      {
        "id": 264340,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-30T20:08:39.588Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Strong disagree that all mummies are zombies.  The original mythology of the zombie from Haitian folktales wasn’t necessarily even dead, just sort of hypnotized to work forever as a worse-than-slave.  Often they would have been buried as if dead, but it was more like they were out into suspended animation with a paralyzing poison.  So your classic plague zombie shouldn’t even really be called that, and Gloomweaver being voodoo-based should be less about then than he is, but I’ll accept that one …I draw the lines at mummies.</p>\n<p>I like the idea that the Atlanteans set the Kraken to guard Atlantis under the assumption that attempts to loot the ruins would be made promptly and consistently, but that didn’t happen, so the Kraken is constantly starving, and that’s why it attacks the lowest HP.  (Of course, C&amp;A immediately contradict that )</p>\n<p>They’re not lizard people you fools!  Read your Conan the Barbarian textbooks, they’re SNAKE people, get it right!</p>\n<p>It’s a cute idea to think that genies are just the Alexa control systems of the lamp and the ring.</p>\n<p>I too prefer to always fight Advanced Powerhound, but haven’t had the courage to deal with Powerhound on Challenge mode.  Frankly it’s obviously never been playtested and is ridiculously hax.</p>",
        "post_number": 8,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-10-31T01:54:30.288Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
